1
00:00:00,201 --> 00:00:01,967
Last video ended with a question:

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:05,340
where is a derivative positive, and where is

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:05,963
it negative?

4
00:00:06,709 --> 00:00:07,397
We'll come back to that.

5
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:09,373
First, look at this curve.

6
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:12,743
Its tangent is flat in two places, at

7
00:00:12,924 --> 00:00:13,765
x equals zero

8
00:00:14,287 --> 00:00:15,570
and at x equals three.

9
00:00:16,353 --> 00:00:19,279
At three, the curve turns, from falling to

10
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:19,660
rising.

11
00:00:20,464 --> 00:00:22,253
But at zero it doesn't turn.

12
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:24,950
It levels off for an instant, then keeps

13
00:00:25,011 --> 00:00:25,333
falling.

14
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:28,797
So what decides whether the curve turns?

15
00:00:29,603 --> 00:00:31,217
Start with what you know from Year 11.

16
00:00:32,222 --> 00:00:34,986
Where the derivative is positive, the tangent slopes

17
00:00:35,167 --> 00:00:37,070
up, and the curve is increasing:

18
00:00:37,632 --> 00:00:40,016
its height goes up as x increases.

19
00:00:40,777 --> 00:00:42,784
Where the derivative is negative, the curve is

20
00:00:42,845 --> 00:00:43,386
decreasing.

21
00:00:44,212 --> 00:00:46,326
Watch the tangent move along this curve.

22
00:00:46,872 --> 00:00:49,176
Its gradient is negative all the way to

23
00:00:49,357 --> 00:00:52,221
x equals three, except for one instant at

24
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:54,245
zero, where it's exactly zero.

25
00:00:55,093 --> 00:00:56,325
After three it's positive.

26
00:00:57,110 --> 00:00:59,397
Let's record just the sign, in a strip

27
00:00:59,538 --> 00:00:59,919
underneath.

28
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:01,877
Two words to keep apart.

29
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:04,812
A stationary point is any point where the

30
00:01:04,832 --> 00:01:07,824
derivative is zero, so the tangent is horizontal.

31
00:01:08,327 --> 00:01:09,153
That's all it says.

32
00:01:10,077 --> 00:01:12,145
A turning point is where the curve changes

33
00:01:12,205 --> 00:01:12,686
direction.

34
00:01:13,287 --> 00:01:16,029
It's either a local maximum, higher than every

35
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:17,310
nearby point on the curve,

36
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:20,652
or a local minimum, lower than every nearby

37
00:01:20,712 --> 00:01:20,912
point.

38
00:01:21,696 --> 00:01:24,192
Local means compared only with points close by.

39
00:01:25,038 --> 00:01:27,087
So the point at three is stationary,

40
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,695
and it's a turning point.

41
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:31,892
The point at zero is stationary, but it's

42
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:32,977
not a turning point.

43
00:01:33,669 --> 00:01:34,661
So what decides it?

44
00:01:35,208 --> 00:01:37,605
The sign of the derivative on each side.

45
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,373
If the curve rises into the point and

46
00:01:40,555 --> 00:01:42,980
falls after it, the sign goes from plus

47
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:43,581
to minus.

48
00:01:44,244 --> 00:01:46,712
Nothing nearby is higher, so it's a local

49
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:47,173
maximum.

50
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:50,404
If it falls in and rises out, that's

51
00:01:50,525 --> 00:01:51,427
minus to plus,

52
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:54,557
and nothing nearby is lower: a local minimum.

53
00:01:55,159 --> 00:01:56,419
And if the sign is the same on

54
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:59,081
both sides, plus and plus, or minus and

55
00:01:59,102 --> 00:02:01,543
minus, the curve keeps going the same way.

56
00:02:02,147 --> 00:02:04,362
That's called a horizontal point of inflection.

57
00:02:04,907 --> 00:02:07,204
It's stationary, but it isn't a turning point.

58
00:02:07,855 --> 00:02:10,081
Why does our curve turn at three but

59
00:02:10,142 --> 00:02:10,823
not at zero?

60
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:14,452
Its derivative is four x squared, times x

61
00:02:14,513 --> 00:02:16,256
minus three, graphed underneath.

62
00:02:16,939 --> 00:02:18,667
The sign of f prime is whether this

63
00:02:18,688 --> 00:02:20,717
graph is above or below the axis.

64
00:02:21,482 --> 00:02:23,571
At three, it crosses the axis, so the

65
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:25,480
sign changes from minus to plus.

66
00:02:26,244 --> 00:02:28,132
At zero, it only touches the axis.

67
00:02:28,635 --> 00:02:30,921
The factor x squared is never negative, so

68
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,205
it doesn't change the sign there,

69
00:02:32,768 --> 00:02:34,993
and x minus three is negative on both

70
00:02:35,055 --> 00:02:35,776
sides of zero.

71
00:02:36,579 --> 00:02:38,888
And because this derivative graph is unbroken, its

72
00:02:38,929 --> 00:02:41,218
sign can only change where it equals zero.

73
00:02:41,922 --> 00:02:44,190
So one test value in each interval is

74
00:02:44,251 --> 00:02:44,451
enough.

75
00:02:45,342 --> 00:02:46,629
Let's turn that into a method.

76
00:02:47,312 --> 00:02:50,016
Find and classify the stationary points of f

77
00:02:50,357 --> 00:02:53,262
of x equals two x cubed, minus nine

78
00:02:53,362 --> 00:02:55,686
x squared, plus twelve x, minus three.

79
00:02:56,448 --> 00:02:59,356
First differentiate, and factorise as far as you

80
00:02:59,397 --> 00:02:59,557
can.

81
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:02,403
f prime of x is six x squared,

82
00:03:02,563 --> 00:03:05,468
minus eighteen x, plus twelve, which is six,

83
00:03:05,749 --> 00:03:08,374
times x minus one, times x minus two.

84
00:03:09,076 --> 00:03:11,501
So f prime is zero at x equals

85
00:03:11,643 --> 00:03:13,266
one and x equals two.

86
00:03:13,969 --> 00:03:16,195
Those two values split the number line into

87
00:03:16,297 --> 00:03:17,018
three intervals.

88
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:20,940
Now test one easy value inside each interval.

89
00:03:21,707 --> 00:03:22,696
Only the sign matters.

90
00:03:23,564 --> 00:03:24,107
At zero,

91
00:03:24,611 --> 00:03:26,364
f prime is twelve, positive.

92
00:03:27,128 --> 00:03:29,319
At one point five, it's minus one point

93
00:03:29,359 --> 00:03:30,364
five, negative.

94
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:33,357
At three, it's twelve, positive.

95
00:03:34,059 --> 00:03:36,749
So f increases for x less than one

96
00:03:37,191 --> 00:03:38,516
and for x greater than two,

97
00:03:39,098 --> 00:03:40,403
and decreases in between.

98
00:03:41,286 --> 00:03:43,333
Plus to minus at one gives a local

99
00:03:43,413 --> 00:03:43,854
maximum,

100
00:03:44,356 --> 00:03:46,263
and minus to plus at two gives a

101
00:03:46,323 --> 00:03:46,965
local minimum.

102
00:03:47,731 --> 00:03:50,027
For the heights, use f, not f prime.

103
00:03:50,850 --> 00:03:51,833
f of one is two,

104
00:03:52,335 --> 00:03:53,498
and f of two is one.

105
00:03:54,155 --> 00:03:55,279
Back to our first curve,

106
00:03:55,842 --> 00:03:57,688
f of x equals x to the fourth,

107
00:03:57,809 --> 00:03:59,073
minus four x cubed.

108
00:03:59,797 --> 00:04:02,762
Its derivative, four x squared times x minus

109
00:04:02,843 --> 00:04:03,162
three,

110
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:06,749
is zero at x equals zero and three.

111
00:04:07,472 --> 00:04:08,395
Test minus one:

112
00:04:09,038 --> 00:04:09,740
minus sixteen.

113
00:04:10,344 --> 00:04:10,886
Test one:

114
00:04:11,511 --> 00:04:11,972
minus eight.

115
00:04:12,659 --> 00:04:13,324
Test four:

116
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:14,413
sixty-four.

117
00:04:15,257 --> 00:04:17,243
Minus, then minus, around zero.

118
00:04:17,866 --> 00:04:19,970
The sign doesn't change, so the point zero,

119
00:04:20,052 --> 00:04:22,397
zero is a horizontal point of inflection.

120
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:26,063
Minus to plus at three gives a local

121
00:04:26,124 --> 00:04:26,444
minimum,

122
00:04:26,966 --> 00:04:29,429
and f of three is eighty-one minus one

123
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:31,572
hundred and eight, which is minus twenty-seven.

124
00:04:32,074 --> 00:04:33,779
Now last video's quotient,

125
00:04:34,302 --> 00:04:36,167
y equals e to the x, over x

126
00:04:36,208 --> 00:04:38,333
plus one, with x not equal to minus

127
00:04:38,395 --> 00:04:38,494
one.

128
00:04:39,157 --> 00:04:41,389
Its derivative is x e to the x,

129
00:04:41,591 --> 00:04:43,259
over x plus one, all squared.

130
00:04:43,942 --> 00:04:45,385
e to the x and the squared bracket

131
00:04:45,426 --> 00:04:47,712
are both positive, so the derivative has the

132
00:04:47,753 --> 00:04:48,294
sign of x:

133
00:04:48,877 --> 00:04:50,501
negative, negative, then positive.

134
00:04:51,063 --> 00:04:53,133
So there's a local minimum at zero, one.

135
00:04:53,757 --> 00:04:56,409
But minus one isn't in the domain, so

136
00:04:56,451 --> 00:04:57,495
it's not a stationary point.

137
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:00,291
It still splits the chart, because the curve

138
00:05:00,332 --> 00:05:00,834
breaks there.

139
00:05:01,418 --> 00:05:03,543
The function decreases on each side of minus

140
00:05:03,685 --> 00:05:05,027
one, but not across it.

141
00:05:05,751 --> 00:05:06,452
At minus two, y

142
00:05:06,955 --> 00:05:09,504
is about minus point one four, and at

143
00:05:09,545 --> 00:05:11,591
minus a half, it's about one point two

144
00:05:11,713 --> 00:05:11,812
one.

145
00:05:12,425 --> 00:05:13,317
Here's a way to picture it.

146
00:05:13,742 --> 00:05:16,049
Turn the signs into arrows, and the arrows

147
00:05:16,290 --> 00:05:17,052
sketch the shape.

148
00:05:17,634 --> 00:05:20,043
Plus is an arrow up, minus is an

149
00:05:20,123 --> 00:05:20,645
arrow down.

150
00:05:21,388 --> 00:05:22,997
Up then down draws a peak.

151
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,268
Down then up draws a valley.

152
00:05:25,871 --> 00:05:27,837
Two arrows the same way draw a step,

153
00:05:28,158 --> 00:05:29,783
the horizontal point of inflection.

154
00:05:30,406 --> 00:05:33,537
Just never join arrows across an excluded value.

155
00:05:33,799 --> 00:05:34,914
There, you lift your pen.

156
00:05:37,693 --> 00:05:38,079
Your turn.

157
00:05:38,608 --> 00:05:41,011
For f of x equals x cubed, minus

158
00:05:41,092 --> 00:05:43,995
three x, find where f is increasing and

159
00:05:44,016 --> 00:05:45,037
where it's decreasing.

160
00:05:45,601 --> 00:05:47,957
Then find and classify its stationary points.

161
00:05:48,582 --> 00:05:49,402
Pause here to answer.

162
00:06:02,155 --> 00:06:04,678
f prime of x is three, times x

163
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,923
minus one, times x plus one,

164
00:06:07,505 --> 00:06:09,788
so it's zero at minus one and one.

165
00:06:10,491 --> 00:06:13,738
Testing minus two, zero and two gives plus,

166
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:14,681
minus, plus.

167
00:06:15,303 --> 00:06:17,948
So f increases for x less than minus

168
00:06:18,049 --> 00:06:20,934
one or greater than one, and decreases in

169
00:06:20,975 --> 00:06:21,355
between.

170
00:06:22,077 --> 00:06:24,602
There's a local maximum at minus one, two,

171
00:06:25,044 --> 00:06:27,269
and a local minimum at one, minus two.

172
00:06:27,953 --> 00:06:28,764
The heights come from f.

173
00:06:29,635 --> 00:06:31,690
Using f prime gives zero every time.

174
00:06:33,359 --> 00:06:33,765
Last one.

175
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:37,101
A function has derivative f prime of x

176
00:06:37,383 --> 00:06:40,630
equals x, times the bracket x minus two,

177
00:06:40,792 --> 00:06:41,232
squared.

178
00:06:41,994 --> 00:06:44,316
Find the x values of its stationary points,

179
00:06:44,718 --> 00:06:47,480
and classify each one, using the sign of

180
00:06:47,721 --> 00:06:48,140
f prime.

181
00:06:48,965 --> 00:06:49,850
Pause here to answer.

182
00:07:00,582 --> 00:07:02,773
f prime is zero at x equals zero

183
00:07:02,914 --> 00:07:03,859
and x equals two.

184
00:07:04,644 --> 00:07:05,469
Test minus one:

185
00:07:06,093 --> 00:07:07,401
minus nine, negative.

186
00:07:08,206 --> 00:07:10,597
Tests at one and three are both positive.

187
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,597
So at zero it's minus to plus, a

188
00:07:13,637 --> 00:07:14,221
local minimum.

189
00:07:14,944 --> 00:07:16,831
At two it's plus on both sides.

190
00:07:17,394 --> 00:07:19,603
The squared bracket doesn't change the sign, so

191
00:07:19,684 --> 00:07:21,672
that's a horizontal point of inflection, not a

192
00:07:21,713 --> 00:07:22,234
turning point.

193
00:07:22,919 --> 00:07:24,752
Don't assume a minimum has to be followed

194
00:07:24,793 --> 00:07:25,357
by a maximum.

195
00:07:27,107 --> 00:07:29,169
So the sign of the derivative on each

196
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:31,912
side tells you whether a stationary point turns.

197
00:07:32,759 --> 00:07:34,130
Next, a bigger question.

198
00:07:34,835 --> 00:07:37,377
Here's attempt one's curve again, with its local

199
00:07:37,438 --> 00:07:38,338
maximum of two.

200
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,202
But on the interval from minus two to

201
00:07:41,263 --> 00:07:41,622
three,

202
00:07:42,224 --> 00:07:44,466
is two the largest value the function reaches?

203
00:07:47,095 --> 00:07:47,958
Here are the key notes.

204
00:07:48,361 --> 00:07:49,908
Pause the video if you need more time

